2026-08-30T11:36Z claude note cross-lingual probe (0266) deviations from the ticket's literal wording, with reasons. (1) Built fresh vectors via a new driver (bench/cross_lingual_probe.mjs, bench/cross_lingual_score.py) rather than reusing 0263's fidelity vectors under 0263-vectors/. Those are a fixed 155-stride UNIFORM sample of 600 passages across the whole 93 022-passage corpus, built for fp32-vs-quantized fidelity comparison on the SAME text at every rung -- they carry no query set, apply no input-template prefix (deliberately, per quant_fidelity.mjs's own docstring), and manual language detection over that exact 600-row sample found only a handful of confirmed non-English rows, not enough to build a topic set. A retrieval probe needs hand-selected topics read for language and content, a real query set with known relevant passages, and the registry's query:/passage: prefixes applied for real -- none of which the fidelity vectors carry. (2) The 4 EN self-check topics show a suspiciously constant hit@10 near 0,50 across every model regardless of quality, traced to the general-distractor sampler picking a mid-document CHUNK rather than the chunk carrying the title -- so for roughly half the self-check queries, the query (the item's title) does not share vocabulary with the embedded passage at all, by construction. This is a limitation of the small EN self-check lane specifically; the VI/DE/RU topics do not share it, since each was hand-read and chosen for a single-language, title-or-topic-matching passage.
